error[operator-consistency]: `==` defined for `Tags` without `hash`
  --> src/OperatorConsistencyPositive.jl:9:1
   |
 9 | Base.:(==)(a::Tags, b::Tags) = a.names == b.names
   | ^^^^^^^^^^ equality without matching `hash`
10 | Base.isequal(a::Tags, b::Tags) = isequal(a.names, b.names)
   | ------------ also defines equality
   |
   = why: `Dict` and `Set` need `isequal(x, y)` to imply equal hashes; Base default `hash` follows `===`, so equal values miss
   = fix: define `Base.hash(x::Tags, h::UInt)` over fields equality compares   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain operator-consistency
   = note: deny from correctness group, library preset
   = note: opt out with `# corset: allow operator-consistency -- <reason>`

error[operator-consistency]: `==` defined for `Point` without `hash`
  --> src/OperatorConsistencyPositive.jl:16:1
   |
16 | Base.:(==)(a::Point{T}, b::Point{T}) where {T} = a.x == b.x
   | ^^^^^^^^^^ equality without matching `hash`
   |
   = why: `Dict` and `Set` need `isequal(x, y)` to imply equal hashes; Base default `hash` follows `===`, so equal values miss
   = fix: define `Base.isequal` and `Base.hash(x::Point, h::UInt)` that apply `isequal` and `hash` to fields `==` compares   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain operator-consistency

error[operator-consistency]: method on `!=`, which Base derives from `==`
  --> src/OperatorConsistencyPositive.jl:26:1
   |
26 | Base.:(!=)(a::Ring, b::Ring) = a.radius != b.radius
   | ^^^^^^^^^^ can disagree with `==`
   |
   = why: Base defines `a != b` as `!(a == b)`; own method can drift from it
   = fix: delete method; define `==` only   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain operator-consistency

error[operator-consistency]: method on `>`, which Base derives from `<`
  --> src/OperatorConsistencyPositive.jl:27:1
   |
27 | Base.:(>)(a::Ring, b::Ring) = a.radius > b.radius
   | ^^^^^^^^^ can disagree with `<`
   |
   = why: Base defines `a > b` as `b < a`; own method can drift from it
   = fix: delete method; define `<` only   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain operator-consistency

error[operator-consistency]: method on `>=`, which Base derives from `<=`
  --> src/OperatorConsistencyPositive.jl:28:1
   |
28 | Base.:(>=)(a::Ring, b::Ring) = a.radius >= b.radius
   | ^^^^^^^^^^ can disagree with `<=`
   |
   = why: Base defines `a >= b` as `b <= a`; own method can drift from it
   = fix: delete method; define `<=` only   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain operator-consistency

error[operator-consistency]: `==` defined for `Span` without `isequal`; compared fields hold floats
  --> src/OperatorConsistencyPositive.jl:34:1
   |
34 | Base.:(==)(a::Span, b::Span) = a.ends == b.ends
   | ^^^^^^^^^^ `isequal` falls back to this `==`
   |
   = why: `0.0 == -0.0` holds, but their hashes differ; `isequal` must tell them apart, as it does for `Float64`
   = fix: define `Base.isequal(a::Span, b::Span)` that applies `isequal` to fields `==` compares   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain operator-consistency

error[operator-consistency]: `hash` for `Account` reads `cache`, which equality ignores
  --> src/OperatorConsistencyPositive.jl:43:10
   |
42 | Base.:(==)(a::Account, b::Account) = a.id == b.id
   | ---------- equality
43 | function Base.hash(account::Account, h::UInt)
   |          ^^^^^^^^^ hashes more than equality compares
   |
   = why: values `isequal` calls equal can differ in `cache`, so their hashes differ and `Dict` keys miss
   = fix: hash only fields equality compares   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain operator-consistency

error[operator-consistency]: `hash` defined for `Node` without `==`
  --> src/OperatorConsistencyPositive.jl:52:1
   |
52 | Base.hash(node::Node, h::UInt) = hash(node.id, h)
   | ^^^^^^^^^ `isequal` still compares by `===`
   |
   = why: `Dict` and `Set` compare `Node` keys by identity; values with equal fields stay separate keys
   = confidence: possible
   = fix: define `==` over fields `hash` reads; delete `hash` when identity is intended   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain operator-consistency

