error[operator-consistency]: 1-argument `hash` method for `Key`
  --> src/OperatorConsistencyPositive.jl:65:1
   |
65 | Base.hash(key::Key, h::UInt = zero(UInt)) = hash(key.id, h)
   | ^^^^^^^^^ replaces Base seed
   |
   = why: Base `hash(x)` calls `hash(x, HASH_SEED)`; this method uses other seed, so `isequal` values of other types can hash differently
   = fix: define 2-argument form only; delete default of `h`   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain operator-consistency

error[operator-consistency]: `isless` for `Job` compares `priority`; equality compares `name`, `priority`
  --> src/OperatorConsistencyPositive.jl:74:1
   |
72 | Base.:(==)(a::Job, b::Job) = a.name == b.name && a.priority == b.priority
   | ---------- equality
73 | Base.hash(job::Job, h::UInt) = hash(job.priority, hash(job.name, h))
74 | Base.isless(a::Job, b::Job) = isless(getfield(a, :priority), b.priority)
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^ orders by other fields than equality
   |
   = why: exactly one of `isequal(x, y)`, `isless(x, y)` and `isless(y, x)` must hold for every `x` and `y`
   = confidence: possible
   = fix: compare fields equality compares; for sort key, sort with `by` instead   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain operator-consistency

